 onClose arg
⍝ Called when a browser session ends, so that a SURVIVING session can prove
⍝ this one was torn down properly (see CBRefresh / F1.CLOSELOG).
⍝
⍝ Two constraints make this function deliberately paranoid:
⍝
⍝  1. closeConnection.aplf:9 calls onClose WITHOUT a trap (endSession.aplf:15
⍝     does wrap it). A signal escaping here would break EWC's own teardown
⍝     on the graceful-close path, so this must be total.
⍝  2. It runs on the Listen thread, not the session thread, while session
⍝     threads may be reading the log — hence the :Hold.

 :Trap 0
     :Hold 'MTESTLOG'
         #.mtestlog.closed,←⊂⍕⎕THIS
     :EndHold
 :EndTrap
